# What 'docker build' tars up and sends to the daemon. Anything not excluded
# here is at least uploaded on every build, and would be baked into the image
# by any COPY that reached it — so this file is the outer of two gates. The
# inner one is the Dockerfile copying only backend/ and the compiled bundle,
# which holds even if a line below is missing.

# --- runtime state: the reason this file exists ---------------------------
# data/ holds the SQLite database — every API key the UI has ever stored —
# alongside the corpus, testsets and evaluation artifacts. logs/ holds app.log
# and the stall dumps. Neither may enter an image.
data/
logs/

# Working notes from the frontend recovery, kept on disk but never published:
# session transcripts that captured live API keys verbatim.
recovery.md
backup.md

# --- not public
design/

# --- regenerated during the build (or before it)
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
# The ** matters: a bare name matches only at the context root, so `__pycache__/`
# alone would let backend/app/__pycache__ through. Measured the hard way — the
# first version of this file used `.DS_Store` and `.pytest_cache/`, and both
# reached a release image from backend/.
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/

# --- VCS / OS / editor
.git/
**/.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
